---
// Addiction IOP, "What is the addiction IOP?" (2026-11-18, replaces the photo carousel). Where the IOP sits between
// traditional outpatient therapy and inpatient rehab, what you keep, and the schedule (CLAUDE.md settled fact 3).
import Icon from "../../Icon.astro";
---
<figure class="gx on-dark" aria-label="The addiction IOP is a higher level of care than traditional outpatient therapy, and unlike inpatient rehab you live at home and keep work, school and family. Monday to Thursday, three hours a day, most people attend 8 to 12 weeks.">
  <p class="gx-t">A higher level of care, without leaving home</p>
  <ol class="gx-lvl">
    <li style="--h:52px"><span class="gx-lvl-bar"></span><b>Traditional outpatient therapy</b></li>
    <li class="is-here" style="--h:100px"><span class="gx-lvl-bar"><Icon name="home" class="h-7 w-7" /></span><b>Addiction IOP</b><small>Structured care several times a week, home every night</small></li>
    <li style="--h:148px"><span class="gx-lvl-bar"></span><b>Inpatient rehab</b></li>
  </ol>
  <p class="gx-t">While you keep up with</p>
  <ul class="gx-tiles is-3">
    <li><span class="gx-i i-b"><Icon name="clipboard" class="h-5 w-5" /></span>Work</li>
    <li><span class="gx-i i-s"><Icon name="compass" class="h-5 w-5" /></span>School</li>
    <li><span class="gx-i i-g"><Icon name="home" class="h-5 w-5" /></span>Family</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="gx-strip"><Icon name="calendar" class="h-5 w-5" /><span><b>Mon–Thu · 3 hours a day</b> · most people attend 8–12 weeks</span></p>
  <figcaption class="gx-foot"><Icon name="check" class="h-4 w-4" />Intensive support that builds independence and accountability</figcaption>
</figure>
